    "gen": {
     "tool": "edge-tts",
     "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
     "rate": "+0%",
     "text": "A single PDF file sitting on a server can generate millions without ever touching a shipping box, because digital products operate on near zero marginal cost per added unit sold. Most people assume scaling a business requires buying physical inventory upfront, but digital files break this rule by costing almost zero dollars to duplicate. You think creating digital income started with modern apps, but back in nineteen ninety six, Bill Gates published his famous essay Content is King, predicting exact digital publishing economics. He laid out how electronic networks would let publishers distribute information worldwide for almost nothing, so the software copy costs nothing to make a million times. Then automated payment gateways arrived to handle the friction, delivering digital files to buyers in under three seconds without a single human worker touching the order. You just upload the asset once, and the server handles a million identical sales while you sleep. The digital money engine was just built on simpler rules."
    }
   }
